        Madhvacharya's Writings and Commentaries
    
    
    
        Commentaries
        Philosophical Treatises
        Other Writings
    
    
        
            Major Commentaries

            Brahma Sutra Bhashya
            This is perhaps Madhvacharya's most significant work, providing a dualistic interpretation of the foundational text of Vedanta, the Brahma Sutras. He emphasizes the distinction between the individual soul and the Supreme Being.

            Bhagavad Gita Bhashya
            In this commentary, Madhvacharya explains the teachings of the Bhagavad Gita through a dualistic lens, highlighting the importance of devotion and the personal relationship between the soul and God.

            Upanishad Bhashya
            Madhvacharya wrote commentaries on several major Upanishads, arguing for the eternal distinction between individual souls and God, and presenting a devotional interpretation of the texts.
        

        
            Philosophical Treatises

            Tattva Vada
            This treatise lays out the tenets of Dvaita philosophy, discussing the nature of reality and the distinction between individual souls and God, emphasizing the role of divine grace in liberation.

            Anu Vada
            In this work, Madhvacharya refutes the arguments of his opponents, particularly those from the Advaita school, elaborating on the differences between Dvaita and Advaita philosophy.
        

        
            Other Writings

            Dasha Shloki
            A short devotional text summarizing the core principles of Madhvacharya's philosophy in ten verses, emphasizing devotion to God and the importance of divine grace.

            Prakritiya Sutra
            This work discusses the nature of reality from the Dvaita perspective, analyzing the relationship between the material world, individual souls, and God.

            Vishnu Tattva Nirnaya
            In this text, Madhvacharya outlines the attributes of Vishnu as the Supreme Being, asserting that devotion to Vishnu is essential for salvation.

            Gita Tattva
            This focused commentary on the Bhagavad Gita emphasizes karma (action) and bhakti (devotion) as pathways to liberation while maintaining the eternal distinction between the soul and God.
        
    
    
